1
00:00:48,461 --> 00:00:54,461
Celestial Avenue is a drama, romance, comedy film directed by Cameron Cairnes.

2
00:01:36,923 --> 00:01:42,923
Kath is looking for love in all the wrong places.

3
00:02:25,384 --> 00:02:31,384
In Chinatown in the middle of a less than successful blind date, she
overhears the soulful Cantonese singing of Ah Gong.

4
00:03:13,846 --> 00:03:19,846
Kath is intrigued.

5
00:04:02,307 --> 00:04:08,307
Is there more to Ah Gong than meets the eye?

6
00:04:50,769 --> 00:04:56,769
Joel, played by Jason Gann.

7
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:45,230
Kath, played by Catherine Moore.

8
00:06:27,692 --> 00:06:33,692
Ah Gong, played by Angus Sampson.

9
00:07:16,153 --> 00:07:22,153
Madame Wong, played by Gabrielle Chan.

10
00:08:04,615 --> 00:08:10,615
Chef Wong, played by Jin Yi.

11
00:08:53,076 --> 00:08:59,076
RBD was a Mexican Latin pop group that gained popularity from
Televisa's telenovela Rebelde (2004–2006).

12
00:09:41,538 --> 00:09:47,538
It was composed of Anahí, Dulce María, Maite Perroni, Alfonso
Herrera, Christopher von Uckermann and Christian Chávez.

13
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,000
The group achieved international success from 2004 until their separation in 2009 and sold over 15 million
records worldwide, making them one of the best-selling Latin music artists of all time.

14
00:11:18,461 --> 00:11:24,461
In November 2004, the group released their debut
studio album, Rebelde, to great success.

15
00:12:06,923 --> 00:12:12,923
In September 2005, the group released their second album, Nuestro Amor, receiving
their first Latin Grammy Award nomination at the 2006 ceremony.

16
00:12:55,384 --> 00:13:01,384
In 2006, the group released their third album, Celestial; this was their
first album to be released simultaneously in all countries.

17
00:13:43,846 --> 00:13:49,846
The album's lead single, "Ser o Parecer", topped the Billboard
Hot Latin Songs chart for two consecutive weeks.

18
00:14:32,307 --> 00:14:38,307
In the same year, the group released their fourth album, and
first English-language project titled Rebels.

19
00:15:20,769 --> 00:15:26,769
In 2007, the group released their fifth album  Empezar Desde Cero,
which was nominated at the Latin Grammy Awards.

20
00:16:09,230 --> 00:16:15,230
In 2009, the group released their sixth and final album, Para Olvidarte De Mí.

21
00:16:57,692 --> 00:17:03,692
RBD officially formed on 30 October 2004, and announced on 15 August 2008,
through a press release, that they would disband on 10 March 2009.

22
00:17:46,153 --> 00:17:52,153
In September 2020, the band announced they would reunite through a virtual show in
December, and their music was released on digital platforms the same month.

23
00:18:34,615 --> 00:18:40,615
Four of the original members returned: Maite Perroni, Anahí,
Christopher von Uckermann and Christian Chávez.

24
00:19:23,076 --> 00:19:29,076
Almost three years later, on 19 January 2023, they announced that all members would return for a
one-off tour, titled Soy Rebelde Tour, with the exception of Alfonso Herrera.

25
00:20:11,538 --> 00:20:17,538
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
